1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,399
Hi Jen.

2
00:00:00,399 --> 00:00:03,308
This is the September plan, in about eight minutes.

3
00:00:03,308 --> 00:00:07,756
It's built around one idea: you're the friend who happens to sell real estate,

4
00:00:07,756 --> 00:00:08,954
and you're from here.

5
00:00:08,954 --> 00:00:11,785
Everything that follows comes from that.

6
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:15,922
Four words before anything else, so nothing tonight sounds like jargon.

7
00:00:15,922 --> 00:00:19,885
A reel is a forty-second video of you talking, filmed on your phone.

8
00:00:19,885 --> 00:00:21,517
It's how strangers find you.

9
00:00:21,517 --> 00:00:24,780
A carousel is a post people swipe through, seven slides.

10
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,937
They save it and send it to a friend.

11
00:00:26,937 --> 00:00:29,151
It's how strangers start to trust you.

12
00:00:29,151 --> 00:00:33,289
The stamp is the small mark on every post with the neighborhood and the

13
00:00:33,289 --> 00:00:33,522
zip.

14
00:00:33,522 --> 00:00:37,485
And the file is three one-page guides you send to anyone who writes.

15
00:00:37,485 --> 00:00:38,068
That's it.

16
00:00:38,068 --> 00:00:39,492
No other terms.

17
00:00:39,492 --> 00:00:42,571
Here's the difference between posting and a system.

18
00:00:42,571 --> 00:00:43,900
A post is a billboard.

19
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,047
A system is a door.

20
00:00:45,047 --> 00:00:49,516
Every post starts with something real happening on your streets this week,

21
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:50,361
never a trend.

22
00:00:50,361 --> 00:00:53,320
Every post has one job: one person writes to you.

23
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:57,366
An address, a question, or just hi, I've been meaning to reach out.

24
00:00:57,366 --> 00:01:00,143
Every reply is already written, in your voice.

25
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:04,256
And what people write back decides what we make next month.

26
00:01:04,256 --> 00:01:05,993
People don't follow an agent.

27
00:01:05,993 --> 00:01:08,449
They follow a person who knows the block.

28
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:09,467
You're from here.

29
00:01:09,467 --> 00:01:13,780
You translate the scary parts, so nobody has to feel dumb to follow you.

30
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,157
And you protect people.

31
00:01:15,157 --> 00:01:17,134
Your own words: I'm here for you.

32
00:01:17,134 --> 00:01:17,972
That's my job.

33
00:01:17,972 --> 00:01:20,848
I do this to protect you and your best interest.

34
00:01:20,848 --> 00:01:23,194
That line ends everything now.

35
00:01:23,194 --> 00:01:25,161
This is the month, not the post.

36
00:01:25,161 --> 00:01:30,386
September is written: the building has to qualify, the train down Van Nuys Boulevard,

37
00:01:30,386 --> 00:01:33,767
the insurance quote before the offer, and just breathe.

38
00:01:33,767 --> 00:01:37,210
Four different subjects, four different kinds of people.

39
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:42,066
October is sketched: sellers, a two million dollar listing in your other voice,

40
00:01:42,066 --> 00:01:45,262
a downsizer, and a client's first year in the house.

41
00:01:45,262 --> 00:01:48,458
What repeats is your face, the stamp, and the close.

42
00:01:48,458 --> 00:01:52,512
The subject never repeats, and neither does who it's for.

43
00:01:52,512 --> 00:01:55,399
How one post becomes a conversation, in six steps.

44
00:01:55,399 --> 00:01:56,727
Something real happens.

45
00:01:56,727 --> 00:01:58,921
You talk for a minute on a voice memo.

46
00:01:58,921 --> 00:02:01,692
We build the reel and the carousel in your look.

47
00:02:01,692 --> 00:02:03,482
It goes out with the door open.

48
00:02:03,482 --> 00:02:07,350
Someone writes, and you answer from a reply that's already written.

49
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,313
Then we listen to what they asked.

50
00:02:09,313 --> 00:02:12,691
The only new work for you is the minute you talk.

51
00:02:12,691 --> 00:02:14,525
We count replies, not likes.

52
00:02:14,525 --> 00:02:18,848
A like, a fire emoji, a new follower, a view from someone in Ohio:

53
00:02:18,848 --> 00:02:19,175
nice.

54
00:02:19,175 --> 00:02:20,354
We don't chase it.

55
00:02:20,354 --> 00:02:24,219
A message with an address, a question about their building,

56
00:02:24,219 --> 00:02:26,969
a we're looking this fall, or a simple hi,

57
00:02:26,969 --> 00:02:30,113
I've been meaning to reach out: that's a person.

58
00:02:30,113 --> 00:02:34,200
That gets the saved reply, the same evening, from you.

59
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:35,918
How this turns into clients.

60
00:02:35,918 --> 00:02:36,655
Four stages.

61
00:02:36,655 --> 00:02:37,760
People who see it.

62
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,803
People who write.

63
00:02:38,803 --> 00:02:39,969
Real conversations.

64
00:02:39,969 --> 00:02:40,522
Closings.

65
00:02:40,522 --> 00:02:44,818
The shape is the same as your referral business, pointed at strangers.

66
00:02:44,818 --> 00:02:47,641
The numbers on the right are yours to fill in.

67
00:02:47,641 --> 00:02:51,324
You already know how many warm conversations become clients.

68
00:02:51,324 --> 00:02:53,902
We'll know the rest after the first month.

69
00:02:53,902 --> 00:02:57,398
Nothing here is promised, and that's on purpose.

70
00:02:57,398 --> 00:03:01,210
In ninety days, this is what the go-to in the Valley looks like on

71
00:03:01,210 --> 00:03:01,788
your grid.

72
00:03:01,788 --> 00:03:03,174
A series people collect.

73
00:03:03,174 --> 00:03:04,445
A stamp on every post.

74
00:03:04,445 --> 00:03:07,565
Your face on the cover, and real Valley places inside.

75
00:03:07,565 --> 00:03:11,782
The same close every time, until it's the thing people quote back to you,

76
00:03:11,782 --> 00:03:15,220
and nobody wonders whether you have time for them.

77
00:03:15,220 --> 00:03:17,143
Your week is about three hours.

78
00:03:17,143 --> 00:03:18,074
One voice memo.

79
00:03:18,074 --> 00:03:20,245
One filming sitting for both reels.

80
00:03:20,245 --> 00:03:24,712
Reply the same evening, in minutes, from a reply that's already written.

81
00:03:24,712 --> 00:03:27,566
And when a post does nothing, nothing happens.

82
00:03:27,566 --> 00:03:28,993
It's not a report card.

83
00:03:28,993 --> 00:03:31,714
We read the month, not the Tuesday.

84
00:03:31,714 --> 00:03:33,840
The slow weeks are part of the plan.

85
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,497
Three closings and a sick kid is most months,

86
00:03:36,497 --> 00:03:38,799
and the system is built for that month.

87
00:03:38,799 --> 00:03:40,511
There's no streak to protect.

88
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:43,168
The file keeps working without you on camera.

89
00:03:43,168 --> 00:03:45,648
A good reel reruns later with a new stamp.

90
00:03:45,648 --> 00:03:48,954
And one voice memo restarts everything when you're back.

91
00:03:48,954 --> 00:03:49,899
No makeup posts.

92
00:03:49,899 --> 00:03:50,980
No guilt.

93
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:51,824
Who does what.

94
00:03:51,824 --> 00:03:55,922
You talk for a minute, film in one sitting, answer the same evening,

95
00:03:55,922 --> 00:03:58,815
and say that's not me whenever a line isn't you.

96
00:03:58,815 --> 00:04:03,034
We find what's real, write it from your memo, build the look, post it,

97
00:04:03,034 --> 00:04:04,782
read every reply, and adjust.

98
00:04:04,782 --> 00:04:06,651
Nothing posts you haven't read.

99
00:04:06,651 --> 00:04:09,672
Every word is yours before it's anyone's.

100
00:04:09,672 --> 00:04:13,546
When someone writes, this is what you hand them: the Valley file.

101
00:04:13,546 --> 00:04:15,632
Three one-page guides in your look.

102
00:04:15,632 --> 00:04:18,076
The four things to read before you write.

103
00:04:18,076 --> 00:04:20,460
The insurance question before the offer.

104
00:04:20,460 --> 00:04:21,354
The eleven p.m.

105
00:04:21,354 --> 00:04:21,950
rate note.

106
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:25,228
And a pinned post on your profile that says start here,

107
00:04:25,228 --> 00:04:29,102
so a stranger who just watched a reel knows exactly who you help.

108
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:30,950
You send it because they wrote.

109
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:32,573
No form, no catch.

110
00:04:32,573 --> 00:04:33,903
What we need from you.

111
00:04:33,903 --> 00:04:36,745
Three phone photos: you on a Van Nuys sidewalk,

112
00:04:36,745 --> 00:04:40,071
you at a condo front door, you holding an H O A packet.

113
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,792
Your real take on the train, as a voice memo.

114
00:04:42,792 --> 00:04:45,029
How many you can film in one sitting.

115
00:04:45,029 --> 00:04:49,147
And your three numbers, so the math on board eight is real.

116
00:04:49,147 --> 00:04:51,480
If you say yes, this is how it runs.

117
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:56,276
This week: the photos, the memo, the numbers, and the first post goes out.

118
00:04:56,276 --> 00:05:00,813
Every week after: one memo from you, two reels and a carousel from us.

119
00:05:00,813 --> 00:05:04,896
Every quarter: a short note to the people who already know you,

120
00:05:04,896 --> 00:05:05,804
in your words.

121
00:05:05,804 --> 00:05:10,081
And what you never do: post daily, chase trends, say top producer,

122
00:05:10,081 --> 00:05:12,705
or write a caption from scratch.

123
00:05:12,705 --> 00:05:14,271
The first post is ready.

124
00:05:14,271 --> 00:05:18,967
Reel one: your credit can be perfect, and the condo still falls through.

125
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:21,446
Then the condo carousel, the next day.

126
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:23,533
Then the reply, already written.

127
00:05:23,533 --> 00:05:25,388
Here's the carousel.

128
00:05:25,388 --> 00:05:25,986
The cover.

129
00:05:25,986 --> 00:05:27,300
You on the front step.

130
00:05:27,300 --> 00:05:28,734
The stamp says Van Nuys.

131
00:05:28,734 --> 00:05:30,826
And the question under the one a.m.

132
00:05:30,826 --> 00:05:34,483
scroll: what if the building is the problem, not me?

133
00:05:34,483 --> 00:05:35,091
Slide two.

134
00:05:35,091 --> 00:05:36,427
You were pre-approved.

135
00:05:36,427 --> 00:05:37,642
The building wasn't.

136
00:05:37,642 --> 00:05:42,988
Since August third, banks check the building's books on almost every regular condo loan.

137
00:05:42,988 --> 00:05:47,422
Four things, mapped: the savings account, twelve months of meeting notes,

138
00:05:47,422 --> 00:05:51,313
the building's own insurance, and who's behind on dues.

139
00:05:51,313 --> 00:05:53,238
Slide three, the savings account.

140
00:05:53,238 --> 00:05:56,211
You open the budget before you look at the balcony.

141
00:05:56,211 --> 00:05:59,301
Ten percent of the building's budget set aside today.

142
00:05:59,301 --> 00:06:03,116
Fifteen percent for loans dated January fourth or later.

143
00:06:03,116 --> 00:06:04,589
Slide four, the dark one.

144
00:06:04,589 --> 00:06:08,358
Somewhere around page four of the meeting notes: roof discussed.

145
00:06:08,358 --> 00:06:11,302
That's a surprise bill, split between every owner,

146
00:06:11,302 --> 00:06:15,268
and it was in the notes months before it hits the mailbox.

147
00:06:15,268 --> 00:06:17,813
Slide five, the building's own insurance.

148
00:06:17,813 --> 00:06:22,533
If your share of one claim goes over fifty thousand dollars, the loan stops.

149
00:06:22,533 --> 00:06:25,203
And the policy has to cover a full rebuild.

150
00:06:25,203 --> 00:06:27,802
The building's policy, not yours.

151
00:06:27,802 --> 00:06:29,866
Slide six, who's behind on dues.

152
00:06:29,866 --> 00:06:33,156
Fifteen percent or more of units sixty days behind,

153
00:06:33,156 --> 00:06:35,349
and no bank lends on the building.

154
00:06:35,349 --> 00:06:36,316
Yours included.

155
00:06:36,316 --> 00:06:38,961
You can pay yours perfectly, every month.

156
00:06:38,961 --> 00:06:41,381
It doesn't change the answer.

157
00:06:41,381 --> 00:06:42,172
And the close.

158
00:06:42,172 --> 00:06:44,262
Send me the address before you write.

159
00:06:44,262 --> 00:06:47,481
We'll read the four documents together and go from there.

160
00:06:47,481 --> 00:06:49,514
Then your line, and my DMs are open.

161
00:06:49,514 --> 00:06:52,493
The sources sit at the bottom of the slide.

162
00:06:52,493 --> 00:06:54,108
The week after: the train.

163
00:06:54,108 --> 00:06:58,022
That torn-up median on Van Nuys Boulevard is a light rail line,

164
00:06:58,022 --> 00:07:01,315
and it doesn't open until December twenty thirty-one.

165
00:07:01,315 --> 00:07:02,681
Same look, same stamp.

166
00:07:02,681 --> 00:07:07,208
The opinion inside is a draft of yours, until you send your own.

167
00:07:07,208 --> 00:07:10,779
Then the insurance quote before the offer, stamped Sherman Oaks.

168
00:07:10,779 --> 00:07:13,848
Fully approved, and the quote still moves your payment.

169
00:07:13,848 --> 00:07:16,742
Every number is sourced on the last slide.

170
00:07:16,742 --> 00:07:20,468
And the saved reply, for the night the first address arrives.

171
00:07:20,468 --> 00:07:22,179
Paste, add their name, send.

172
00:07:22,179 --> 00:07:23,645
That's the whole system.

173
00:07:23,645 --> 00:07:27,494
Everything works out exactly the way it's supposed to.
